{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "0DTR", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-automorphism-groups}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ab5c6166f2904044c829de8b34f716a396869521a9a576050b5b24ca17f58a47", "source_text": "Automorphism groups", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7534205be63b954e946924a6abb7330e92a1107bf11071ec5c679dd713aa4cab", "unit_id": "tag:0DTR:title"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0DTR", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$x \\in |\\mathcal{X}|$", "MATH_0003": "$x : \\Spec(k) \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0004": "$G_x/k$", "MATH_0005": "$x$", "MATH_0006": "$$\nG_x = \\mathit{Isom}_\\mathcal{X}(x, x) =\n\\Spec(k) \\times_\\mathcal{X} \\mathcal{I}_\\mathcal{X}\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$x$", "MATH_0008": "$\\Spec(k)$", "MATH_0009": "$k'/k$", "MATH_0010": "$x' : \\Spec(k') \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0011": "$G_x$", "MATH_0012": "$\\Spec(k')$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:1b90cd8466beeacf88090fcdd198b7eca82b8bca9356a37172c1f34754cdfe8d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:78ec8efa37f40c4729633f3d3336dc986577c46912c83a14b489108f1526b11c", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be an algebraic stack. Let <MATH_0002>\ncorrespond to <MATH_0003>. In this situation we\noften use the phrase\n``let <MATH_0004> be the automorphism group algebraic space of <MATH_0005>''.\nThis just means that\n<MATH_0006>\nis the group algebraic space of automorphism of <MATH_0007>. This is a\ngroup algebraic space over <MATH_0008>. If <MATH_0009> is an extension of fields\nthen the automorphism group algebraic space of the induced morphism\n<MATH_0010> is the base change of <MATH_0011>\nto <MATH_0012>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:db156ba56b1d493fd96891402da170e6881f6978a23505e40a36647c4cbbea48", "unit_id": "tag:0DTR:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0DTR", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$G_x$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Delta : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{X} \\times \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\Delta : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{X} \\times \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{I}_\\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{I}_\\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{I}_\\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\item", "STRUCT_0007": "\\item", "STRUCT_0008": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-automorphism-group-scheme}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:6bcff475bf652c7b30f50a558dd7f006d37b31c5bdd1eccea6c7937cb63ea037", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ef7696afd49cd06fc8ace5f7837d5064145d6d17d0fbce38c2c82321f4a89d39", "source_text": "In the situation above <MATH_0001> is a scheme if one of the following\nholds\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0002>\nis quasi-separated\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0003>\nis locally separated,\n<STRUCT_0004> <MATH_0004> is quasi-DM,\n<STRUCT_0005> <MATH_0005>\nis quasi-separated,\n<STRUCT_0006> <MATH_0006>\nis locally separated, or\n<STRUCT_0007> <MATH_0007>\nis locally quasi-finite.\n<STRUCT_0008>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3a937816a7f6a755eb5485394d2f7e51b0501a8e8752af51179143a04985049a", "unit_id": "tag:0DTS:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0DTR", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Rightarrow$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Rightarrow$", "MATH_0003": "$\\Rightarrow$", "MATH_0004": "$G_x$", "MATH_0005": "$G_x$", "MATH_0006": "$G_x$", "MATH_0007": "$G_x$", "MATH_0008": "$G_x$", "MATH_0009": "$G_x \\to \\Spec(k)$", "MATH_0010": "$G_x$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-diagonal-diagonal}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{decent-spaces-section-reasonable-decent}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{decent-spaces-lemma-locally-separated-decent}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{spaces-more-groupoids-lemma-group-scheme-over-field-separated}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{spaces-more-groupoids-proposition-group-space-scheme-over-field}", "REF_0006": "\\ref{spaces-over-fields-lemma-locally-quasi-finite-over-field}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:647e596abc0bae57f5f12834ea901d00a7f3f12712a2bb1c4993c38223bb0b7e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c516100425c0d7d0eafda568a5138afaf9a903ccd5ba461efeb605dbf72770e8", "source_text": "Observe that (1) <MATH_0001> (4), (2) <MATH_0002> (5), and\n(3) <MATH_0003> (6) by\nLemma <REF_0001>.\nIn case (4) we see that <MATH_0004> is a quasi-separated\nalgebraic space and in case (5) we see that <MATH_0005>\nis a locally separated algebraic space.\nIn both cases <MATH_0006> is a decent algebraic space\n(Decent Spaces, Section <REF_0002> and\nLemma <REF_0003>).\nThen <MATH_0007> is separated by More on Groupoids in Spaces, Lemma\n<REF_0004>\nwhereupon we conclude that <MATH_0008> is a scheme by\nMore on Groupoids in Spaces, Proposition\n<REF_0005>.\nIn case (6) we see that <MATH_0009> is locally quasi-finite\nand hence <MATH_0010> is a scheme by\nSpaces over Fields, Lemma\n<REF_0006>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a48951b56e82076e215a92dd25af4e2118c3c94560b5413e0bb9a0c48cfef84b", "unit_id": "tag:0DTS:proof"}
